Numerical constraints:
   usablegc >= 0.0
   usablevc >= 0.0
   0.1 kg/L <= density <= 3.0 kg/L   Better if 0.1 <= density <= 0.6 kg/L
   0.3 <= porosity <= 0.9            Better if 0.7 <= porosity <= 0.9
   Ri > 0.0                          Better if 5 angstroms < Ri < 15 angstroms
   ssa > 0.0                         Better if ssa >= 4000 m^2/g
   specific pore volume > 0.0        Better if specific pore volume >= 1.0 cm^3/g

Qualitative constraints:
   SSA and specific pore volume are, in general, inversely proportional 
   to the density.
   Porosity is, in general, inversely proportional to the density.
   If the porosity is high then, Ri is usually large.
   SSA and porosity are correlated. The dependence of SSA on the 
   porosity is approximately linear.

Densities of materials at 15-25 ºC and one athmosphere of pressure:
   The density of Lead is 11.3 kg/L
   The densest natural material is Osmium: 22.6 kg/L
   The densities of MOFs are within the interval 0.1-4.1 kg/L


Escalado:
column='density', minimum=0.001, maximum=3.0
column='porosity', minimum=0., maximum=1.
column='Ri', minimum=0.0, maximum=20.
column='ssa', minimum=0.0, maximum=10000.
column='specific', minimum=0.0, maximum=2.
